   184	### 1.6 What D665 prints beside, with its tool and input
   185	
   186	| What | Status | Tool and input |
   187	|---|---|---|
   188	| D400 accounting, all three passes (`stage_a/accounting.py`) | **Hard:** figure ranges meet end to end; the favourable end is stable; the due day agrees across all three sends for ≥ 90% of eligible questions. A failure is a release blocker reported with the verdict. Lines 1–5: reported | The new system's three draws. The reader lines use the October two-family Stage A reading on every draw |
   189	| Step 2's three lines (D427; PRD §5) | **Hard**, like D400's code-decided parts: a failed line is a release blocker reported with the verdict. Pass: earlier version found ≥ 90%; clearly wrong merges ≤ 2%; no fewer later details than no merging. Each decided on its point estimate, intervals printed | The Step 2 log §12 method on draw 1 of the new system: recall over 100 records with a labelled earlier version (stratified random); blind review of 200 random merges; the no-merge dossier comparison on 30 groups. The sample sizes are a recorded design choice |
   190	| D431's frozen-reference reading, 07-01 to 07-14 | Printed beside | The D395 method (`clean-arch/unseeded-2026-11-10/MATCHING-v2.md`: the seven graded questions against the frozen judgement gold) on **both** systems' draws as they stood at 07-14 |
   191	| Proposed absolute floors | Printed beside | Coverage ≥ 80%, trivia ≤ 20% and supported ≥ 90% come from this comparison's cards. Wrong citations ≤ 5% and zero answer-changing omissions need source-first readings this plan does not run: printed as **not measured** (agreed in the council before the send) |
   192	
   193	### 1.7 Long-run risk, checked at $0
   194	
   195	- **The old judge's request size.** poc-v118's `evidence_in_view` (`views/judging.py:41`) shows every arrival since the fifth most recent
   196	  judgement, which is unbounded.
   197	  - Proxy: the sealed v34 ledger (07-01 to 08-28, 8 halt files).
   198	  - Code computes the size of every request v118's rule would build on it.
   199	  - If any exceeds the model's input limit or v34's halting size (292 KB), the risk is reported before the send.
   200	- **The same for the new judge,** on the carried fortnight, scaled.
   201	
   202	### 1.8 Preflight
   203	
   204	- Every stored answer of the latest runs of both systems goes through the current checks (AGENTS §5).
   205	- Both launchers run dry over two days with every code change in place.
   206	
   207	**Freeze review:** the council reads §1's artifacts, proofs and outputs. A finding is fixed and the review repeated. The paid stages start
   208	when it finds nothing serious.
   209	
   210	## 2. Stage 1: the slice
   211	
   212	- **What runs:** one draw of each system, 07-01 to 07-07 (about 98 articles), each on its own ledger.
   213	- **Passes when:**
   214	  - both draws complete;
   215	  - the new system's Step 1 averages ≤ 51 s and ≤ $0.0153 an article (1.5 × the measured 34 s and $0.0102);
   216	  - every answer-choice request was checked at the transport, and every archive shows astra;
   217	  - production's days are complete.
   218	- **On a failure:** fix the launcher only, then rerun. Anything else goes to the council, and then to Alex.

